Object oriented concepts in Kotlin
- Classes and primary constructors — define object blueprints and initialize properties.
- Properties and methods — data and behavior belonging to classes.
- Visibility modifiers — control access: public, private, protected, internal.
- Inheritance and open keyword — extend classes; classes are final by default.
- Abstract classes and methods — provide partial implementations for subclasses.
- Interfaces — define contracts with default implementations.
- Data classes — concise holders for immutable data with generated equals/hash/toString/copy.
- Sealed classes — restricted class hierarchies for exhaustive when expressions.
- Enum classes — fixed set of constants with optional properties and behaviour.
- Companion objects and factory methods — static-like members and construction helpers.
- Object singletons — single-instance objects with initialization.
- Delegation and by keyword — delegate implementation to another object or property.
- Secondary constructors and init blocks — additional initialization paths.
- Backing fields and custom getters/setters — control property access logic.
- Generics and variance — type-parameterized classes and in/out variance for safe subtyping.
- Visibility with constructors — control who can instantiate a class.
